      "id": "9au73g4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Lengthiest Written Constitution"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Indian Constitution is the lengthiest written constitution in the world due to geographical, historical, and structural factors.",
        "It represents a unique synthesis of parliamentary sovereignty from Britain and judicial supremacy from the USA.",
        "It establishes a federal structure with a strong centralizing tendency, often described as a quasi-federal state.",
        "Fundamental Rights are enforceable by courts, whereas Directive Principles of State Policy are non-justiciable guidelines for state policy.",
        "Single citizenship is provided to foster national unity, contrasting with the dual citizenship model of federal states like the USA."
      ],
      "id": "imc1ud6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "17zylge"
    },
